After some time, you are already tied up by the pole with the totem. The savages continue their dancing around it, and the expressions on their faces you don't like at all.

Suddenly, there is a clap of a shot. The savage nearest to you snatches at his chest, then takes his blood-stained hand to his eyes and falls dead. Several more shots sound, finding their targets. The savages begin to panic. Some of them fall on the ground shaking, covering their heads with their hands. But most of them run away, dropping their weapons. Soon, only corpses and sparsely scattered people trembling in fear can be seen on the clearing.